csv NEWS - History of user-visible changes

Version 1.2.0 (December 2025)

  * New command: csv pick [-a] [-f file] row1 row2 ...
    - Select specific data rows by number (1-indexed)
    - Use -a to include header (and comments) in output
    - Supports stdin input when -f is not specified

  * Changed wc output format to "Rows: N  Columns: N  Bytes: N"

  * The -a flag now consistently includes comment lines with the header
    across all commands (head, tail, wc, cut, pick)

  * Added --version (-V) option to display version information

Version 1.1.0 (November 2025)

  * Added POSIX-style +N options for head and tail commands:
    - csv tail +N: Start from row N and print to end (1-indexed)
    - csv head +N: Show all but last N data rows

  * This follows the POSIX tail convention where +N means
    "start from line N" rather than "last N lines"

Version 1.0.0 (November 2025)

  * Initial release with four commands:
    - csv head: Show first n rows
    - csv tail: Show last n rows
    - csv wc: Count rows, columns, and bytes
    - csv cut: Select specific columns by name

  * Features:
    - Row-aware CSV parsing (handles quoted fields with newlines)
    - Comment line support (lines starting with #)
    - Consistent -a flag for including headers
    - stdin/stdout support for pipelines
    - GNU-style installation with Makefile
